course: dictionary
lesson: 6130
title: Mighty and its many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. The word mighty can mean very strong, very big, or very impressive. The words around it show you which meaning the writer wants. «Babylon had mighty walls» tells you the walls were huge and strong, so mighty means big and impressive here.
explain: Look at the word before and after it. In «Together they faced the mighty Persian Empire», the empire was large and powerful, so mighty means strong and powerful. Ask yourself: which meaning makes the sentence sensible? Then test it by putting your meaning in place of the word.
explain: Mighty can also be a friendly word for very, but only in some places. Aoife says «the craic was mighty» in Ireland, meaning the fun was great. Maddie's «sweet as» means the same thing in Australia. In the US South, «That's mighty kind of you» means «That's very kind of you.» Mighty is a little old-fashioned, so it often sounds grand.
fact: Mighty means very strong or powerful.
fact: Mighty also means very big and impressive, as in «a mighty river» or «a mighty oak».
fact: The comparative forms are mightier and mightiest.
fact: In the saying «The pen is mightier than the sword», mightier means stronger. It means words and ideas can be more powerful than fighting.
fact: «High and mighty» means acting proud and bossy, not strong or tall.
exercise: «The mighty river flooded the fields.» What does mighty mean here? | *Very big and powerful | Cold and icy | Very quiet and still | Made of wood
exercise: Aoife says «the craic was mighty». What does mighty mean here? | *Really great, very good fun | Wet and muddy | Very scary | Not very much at all
exercise: Which word could replace mighty in «That's mighty kind of you»? | heavy | blue | *very | quiet
test: «The mighty oak stood tall in the park.» Which meaning fits best? | Very dark and wet | *Very big and strong | Very small and thin | Very old and broken
test: Which saying means that words and ideas can be stronger than fighting? | Mighty hands make light work | The sword is sharper than the pen | *The pen is mightier than the sword | High and mighty is best
exam: «High and mighty» means someone is | a long way away | *acting proud and bossy | very tall and strong | very kind and gentle
